WHICH ONE APPLIES TO YOU

Use the GPL if you are an individual, a hobbyist, a researcher, an
open-source project, or anyone willing to release their own derivative
work under the GPL as well.

Buy a commercial license if you want to use Kestrel, or anything built
from it, inside a proprietary or closed-source product, or in enterprise
infrastructure, without the obligations the GPL places on you.

The obligation people most often miss: the GPL applies when you CONVEY
the software to someone else, not when you merely use it. Running
Kestrel inside your company, unmodified and not distributed outside it,
does not by itself require you to publish anything. Shipping a product
that contains it, or a modified version of it, does.

Using Kestrel as a tool to produce something is not covered by either
license. Documents, macros and output you create with it are yours.

